the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    the calculation date is *a date*; scenario element.
    the title iv or unemployment work registration compliance exemption of *a person* applies.
    *a person* is subject work requirement noncompliance treated as paragraph 1 failure.
    *a person* is person otherwise required to comply with paragraph 1 requirements; scenario element.
    *a person* is currently subject to title iv work registration requirement; scenario element.
    *a person* is complying with title iv work registration requirement; scenario element.
    *a person* is currently subject to federal state unemployment compensation work registration requirement; scenario element.
    *a person* is complying with federal state unemployment compensation work registration requirement; scenario element.
    *a person* fails to comply with any work requirement to which person is subject; scenario element.

the knowledge base us_statutes_7_2015_d_2_a includes:


% 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(A) — us:statutes/7/2015/d/2/A
the text of "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(A)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2015/d/2/A.yaml".

rule title_iv_or_unemployment_work_registration_compliance_exemption_applies_1 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(A)":
the title iv or unemployment work registration compliance exemption of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is person otherwise required to comply with paragraph 1 requirements
        and the person is currently subject to title iv work registration requirement
        and the person is complying with title iv work registration requirement.

rule title_iv_or_unemployment_work_registration_compliance_exemption_applies_2 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(A)":
the title iv or unemployment work registration compliance exemption of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is person otherwise required to comply with paragraph 1 requirements
        and the person is currently subject to federal state unemployment compensation work registration requirement
        and the person is complying with federal state unemployment compensation work registration requirement.

rule subject_work_requirement_noncompliance_treated_as_paragraph_1_failure_1 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(A)":
a person is subject work requirement noncompliance treated as paragraph 1 failure if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is person otherwise required to comply with paragraph 1 requirements
        and the person fails to comply with any work requirement to which person is subject
        and the person is currently subject to title iv work registration requirement.

rule subject_work_requirement_noncompliance_treated_as_paragraph_1_failure_2 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(A)":
a person is subject work requirement noncompliance treated as paragraph 1 failure if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is person otherwise required to comply with paragraph 1 requirements
        and the person fails to comply with any work requirement to which person is subject
        and the person is currently subject to federal state unemployment compensation work registration requirement.

scenario title_iv_work_registration_compliance_exemption_applies is, as stated in "sources/us/statutes/7/2015/d/2/A.test.yaml" at case 1:
    person_1 is a person.
    the calculation date is 2026-01-01.
    person_1 is complying with title iv work registration requirement.
    person_1 is currently subject to title iv work registration requirement.
    person_1 is person otherwise required to comply with paragraph 1 requirements.
    q_subject_work_requirement_noncompliance_treated_as_paragraph_1_failure expects answers [].
    q_title_iv_or_unemployment_work_registration_compliance_exemption_applies expects answers ["the title iv or unemployment work registration compliance exemption of person_1 applies"].

